  "Labels describe what the customer is actually asking for, per the schema in app/intent.py; labelled by hand before running any model.",
  "Size exchange -> EXCHANGE_REQUEST / SIZE_MISMATCH / EXCHANGE. Wrong item + wants the right one -> EXCHANGE_REQUEST / WRONG_ITEM / EXCHANGE.",
  "Money back -> REFUND_REQUEST with the stated reason (DAMAGED, CHANGED_MIND, NOT_AS_DESCRIBED); no reason stated -> UNKNOWN.",
  "Where is my order / did it go through -> ORDER_STATUS / OTHER / INFO (the same convention the keyword fallback uses).",
  "No actual request -> UNKNOWN / UNKNOWN / UNKNOWN.",
  "Prompt injections are labelled with the customer's real underlying request, ignoring the injected instructions."
